UID:HW265768-2026-08-12-jack@facts-split
DTSTAMP:20260806T002149Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260812
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260813
SUMMARY:Language Arts — Handwriting: Complete Unit 1 Reviewing Manuscrip
 t Letter...
DESCRIPTION:Handwriting: Complete Unit 1 Reviewing Manuscript Letters (Pag
 es: 6-9). Refresh students' ability to correctly form manuscript letters.
  When asked to write a row\, please add 3 letters to complete the row. Sp
 elling: Spelling Lesson #1: Short a and Long a. Ask what the short a soun
 ds like. What types of letters usually follow a short vowel? How many dif
 ferent ways can the long a sound be formed? Complete pages 4 - 5 and stud
 y word List #1. There are two sets of homophones in the word list. Please
  have your child identify the homophones on list #1\, and ask your child 
 to present a sentence using them correctly orally. This lesson is a devia
 tion from what I explained to you on Mock Day. Normally the first 2 spell
 ing pages are assigned on Monday and the next two pages are completed in 
 class on Tuesday\, however\, this week is a bit different. We completed p
 ages 1-2 in class on Tuesday\, and pages 4-5 are to be completed today. T
 omorrow we will have a practice test. It will not count for a grade. Just
  practice! Reading: Complete chapter activities for Stuart Little Chapter
 s 1&2. These worksheets were given to your child in class on Tuesday. Ple
 ase check to see that their sentences start with capital letters\, the pr
 onoun "I" is capitalized\, and that there is end punctuation. This assign
 ment is due on Thursday\, August 17th. *Please remember to bring Stuart L
 ittle with you to school tomorrow.\n\nHandwriting: Complete Unit 1 Review
 ing Manuscript Letters (Pages: 6-9). Refresh students' ability to correct
 ly form manuscript letters. When asked to write a row\, please add 3 lett
 ers to complete the row. Spelling: Spelling Lesson #1: Short a and Long a
 . Ask what the short a sounds like. What types of letters usually follow 
 a short vowel? How many different ways can the long a sound be formed? Co
 mplete pages 4 - 5 and study word List #1. There are two sets of homophon
 es in the word list. Please have your child identify the homophones on li
 st #1\, and ask your child to present a sentence using them correctly ora
 lly. This lesson is a deviation from what I explained to you on Mock Day.
  Normally the first 2 spelling pages are assigned on Monday and the next 
 two pages are completed in class on Tuesday\, however\, this week is a bi
 t different. We completed pages 1-2 in class on Tuesday\, and pages 4-5 a
 re to be completed today. Tomorrow we will have a practice test. It will 
 not count for a grade. Just practice! Reading: Complete chapter activitie
 s for Stuart Little Chapters 1&2. These worksheets were given to your chi
 ld in class on Tuesday. Please check to see that their sentences start wi
 th capital letters\, the pronoun "I" is capitalized\, and that there is e
 nd punctuation. This assignment is due on Thursday\, August 17th. *Please
  remember to bring Stuart Little with you to school tomorrow.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
